# KWin's screen locker in Hearth's KWin session (docs/KWIN-INPUT.md). Mantel decides when to lock (Super+L, the power
# menu, Settings › Sign-in › Lock when waking, idle): Lock.qml asks KWin's locker, so KWin itself never locks on its
# own (that would be a setting changing by itself) and the screen it shows is Hearth's (kwin-lock/, the Plasma shell package
# org.hearth.mantel-lock that PLASMA_DEFAULT_SHELL names in KWin's session). Read from XDG_CONFIG_DIRS: nothing here is written to your files.
# [$i] makes each key fixed (KConfig's "immutable"): a ~/.config/kscreenlockerrc left from KDE Plasma (1.13) with
# Autolock or LockOnResume on can't turn KWin's own locking back on, which would skip hearth-lockcheck and could lock
# a handheld out. Your file isn't changed; Hearth tells you once which of its keys aren't used (hearth-your-desktop
# kwin-overrides, the keys listed there as LOCKED) and Mantel's Settings › Sign-in decides when to lock.
[Daemon]
Autolock[$i]=false
LockOnResume[$i]=false
Timeout[$i]=0

